            <title>[LU-21055] conf-sanity test_160: format failed: rc = 10, zpool export of lustre-ost2 reports pool is busy</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21055</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;conf-sanity test_160 failed in its reformat step, before the test body ran, on review-dne-zfs-part-3 (ZFS OSS, 8 OSTs formatted in parallel on one node).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;format_ost2 reported "cannot export 'lustre-ost2': pool is busy" from the "zpool export" run right after mkfs.lustre created lustre-ost2 on the OSS (ssh exit 1, "format_ost2 failed: rc = 10"). The other OSTs formatted without error, and formatall ended with "format failed: rc = 10", so the test returned 10.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/3120c10a-cdd3-4ded-8130-3728d0de19c7" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/3120c10a-cdd3-4ded-8130-3728d0de19c7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test set: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/11a795e6-8ab9-4b2a-98b0-f64fc69b9a25" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/11a795e6-8ab9-4b2a-98b0-f64fc69b9a25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Tested: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11081" title="LFSCK support for DoM file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11081"&gt;LU-11081&lt;/a&gt; lfsck patch (&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/66841" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66841&lt;/a&gt; ps18), which does not touch conf-sanity, the format code or ZFS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rate: 1 failure in 2308 review-dne-zfs-part-3 runs on master over 30 days (this change passed 9 of 9 other runs). Likely a race between the parallel pool creation and "zpool export" of a pool still held open (udev or a concurrent zpool operation); format_ost does not retry the export.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-66841-ps18-d1e686e31805 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/66841" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66841&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
